### Description

Create an IP whitelist record so the specified hosts take effect for script execution and/or file distribution, either for all businesses or for the selected businesses. The caller must have permission to create an IP whitelist.

When both a host ID and a cloud area plus IP are provided, the host ID is used. When only a cloud area and IP are provided, they must match exactly one host; otherwise the request fails and no whitelist record is created.

### Request Parameters

#### Body Parameters

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|------|------|------|------|
| all_scope | boolean | No | Whether the record applies to all businesses. Allowed values: true (all businesses), false (only businesses in scope_list, default false). scope_list is ignored when this is true |
| scope_list | array | No | Businesses the record applies to. At least one item is required when all_scope is false. Ignored when all_scope is true |
| host_list | array | Yes | Hosts to add. At least one host is required. Duplicate hosts keep the first occurrence |
| remark | string | Yes | Remark. Cannot be empty |
| action_scope_list | array | Yes | Action scopes. At least one item is required. Allowed values: SCRIPT_EXECUTE (script execution), FILE_DISTRIBUTION (file distribution). Both may be sent together. Duplicate values are removed |

##### scope_list[] element

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|------|------|------|------|
| bk_scope_type | string | Yes | Resource scope type. Allowed values: biz (business), biz_set (business set), tenant_set (tenant set) |
| bk_scope_id | string | Yes | Resource scope ID corresponding to bk_scope_type. It is a business ID, business set ID, or tenant set ID |

##### host_list[] element

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|------|------|------|------|
| bk_host_id | long | No | CMDB host ID. Must be a positive integer. When set, this host is used and bk_cloud_id and ip on the same element are ignored |
| bk_cloud_id | long | No | Cloud area ID, greater than or equal to 0. 0 is the direct-connect area. Required together with ip when bk_host_id is absent |
| ip | string | No | Host IPv4. Required together with bk_cloud_id when bk_host_id is absent. If the cloud area and IP do not match exactly one host, the request fails and nothing is created |

##### action_scope_list[] element

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|------|------|------|------|
| (element) | string | Yes | Action scope. Allowed values: SCRIPT_EXECUTE (script execution), FILE_DISTRIBUTION (file distribution) |

### Request Example

- POST

Example 1: target selected businesses by host ID

```json
{
    "all_scope": false,
    "scope_list": [
        {
            "bk_scope_type": "biz",
            "bk_scope_id": "2"
        },
        {
            "bk_scope_type": "biz_set",
            "bk_scope_id": "3"
        }
    ],
    "host_list": [
        {
            "bk_host_id": 101
        },
        {
            "bk_host_id": 102
        }
    ],
    "remark": "allow script execute and file distribution",
    "action_scope_list": [
        "SCRIPT_EXECUTE",
        "FILE_DISTRIBUTION"
    ]
}
```

Example 2: target all businesses by cloud area and IP

```json
{
    "all_scope": true,
    "host_list": [
        {
            "bk_cloud_id": 0,
            "ip": "127.0.0.1"
        }
    ],
    "remark": "allow all businesses",
    "action_scope_list": [
        "SCRIPT_EXECUTE"
    ]
}
```

### Response Examples

#### Failure

{% include '_generic_v4_error_resp.md.j2' %}

If the host cannot be identified uniquely, or the page, action scope, or business scope is invalid, the HTTP status is 400 and error.code is INVALID_ARGUMENT. If the caller cannot create an IP whitelist, the HTTP status is 403 and error.code is NO_PERMISSION.

#### Success

```json
# http status=200
{
    "data": {
        "id": 1001,
        "bk_cloud_id": 0,
        "host_list": [
            {
                "bk_host_id": 101,
                "bk_cloud_id": 0,
                "ip": "127.0.0.1"
            }
        ],
        "action_scope_list": [
            "SCRIPT_EXECUTE",
            "FILE_DISTRIBUTION"
        ],
        "all_scope": false,
        "scope_list": [
            {
                "bk_scope_type": "biz",
                "bk_scope_id": "2",
                "name": "demo-biz"
            }
        ],
        "remark": "allow script execute and file distribution",
        "creator": "admin",
        "create_time": 1735689600000,
        "last_modifier": "admin",
        "last_modify_time": 1735689600000
    }
}
```

### Response Parameters

{% include '_generic_v4_response.md.j2' %}

#### data

| Field | Type | Description |
|------|------|------|
| id | long | Whitelist record ID |
| bk_cloud_id | long | Summary cloud area ID of the record. When hosts in the same record belong to different cloud areas, use bk_cloud_id of each host in host_list. Omitted when the record has no host |
| host_list | array | Whitelist hosts |
| action_scope_list | array | Action scopes. Allowed values: SCRIPT_EXECUTE (script execution), FILE_DISTRIBUTION (file distribution) |
| all_scope | boolean | Whether the record applies to all businesses. Allowed values: true (all businesses), false (only businesses in scope_list) |
| scope_list | array | Businesses the record applies to. Empty array when all_scope is true |
| remark | string | Remark |
| creator | string | Creator |
| create_time | long | Creation time, Unix timestamp in milliseconds |
| last_modifier | string | Last modifier |
| last_modify_time | long | Last modification time, Unix timestamp in milliseconds |

##### host_list[] element

| Field | Type | Description |
|------|------|------|
| bk_host_id | long | CMDB host ID |
| bk_cloud_id | long | Cloud area ID |
| ip | string | Host IPv4. Omitted when the host has no IPv4 |
| ipv6 | string | Host IPv6. Omitted when the host has no IPv6 |

##### action_scope_list[] element

| Field | Type | Description |
|------|------|------|
| (element) | string | Action scope. Allowed values: SCRIPT_EXECUTE (script execution), FILE_DISTRIBUTION (file distribution) |

##### scope_list[] element

| Field | Type | Description |
|------|------|------|
| bk_scope_type | string | Resource scope type. Allowed values: biz (business), biz_set (business set), tenant_set (tenant set). May be omitted when the business has been deleted |
| bk_scope_id | string | Resource scope ID. May be omitted when the business has been deleted |
| name | string | Name of the business, business set, or tenant set. A placeholder text is returned when the business has been deleted |
